[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Read by cause rather than by subject
line, its reports hold three problems. Each one now has its own ticket.

<Callout>
Closed 5 October. Engineering fixed the parser and retired the booking-v3 form. Nothing has fixed the
one-day move: if those reports keep coming, reopen its ticket.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads dates month first.** Every tenant on file writes the day first,
so 7 April becomes 4 July. This covers reports from every tenant, through the app, email and the
booking-v2 form.

**`hint`: booking-v3 tells day-first tenants to type the month first.** Its date field prints
`MM/DD/YYYY`. People follow the hint, and the form reads what they type day first. This covers only
reports sent through the booking form of a booking-v3 tenant. Fixing the parser does not fix it.

**`one-day move`: the date moves by one day, not by a swap.** The month stays and the day shifts by
one, and it depends on where the reader is ("Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got
Monday."). This looks like a time-zone conversion, not the parser. The desk had already marked
these reports as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`). The desk files a report by its tenant, so they
stay counted under `parser` too, footnoted under the table.

## Outcome

- `parser`: fixed, `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`. Ticket closed as completed.
- `hint`: won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired. Ticket closed as not planned.
- `one-day move`: closed with #4471 as not planned. Neither change touches it.

## Why one ticket hid three

- [Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on subject line alone. All three
  problems produce the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Month and day swapped?"), so they
  were merged into one ticket.
- The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser, not the tenant's locale and form. It
  disagrees with the cause on many reports (the column above), so counting by tag is wrong too.
- The ticket export repeats some reports across pages. Counted once by id.

## For the desk

- A day/month swap reported after 5 October is a regression of the parser fix: open a new ticket.
- Send reports of a date off by one day to the one-day-move ticket and reopen it, whatever their subject says.

